---

## 1. How the grammar works (important context)

- `grammar.js` is the source grammar (tree-sitter DSL, ~1,600 lines).
- `tree-sitter generate` compiles it into `src/parser.c` (generated, ~55 MB),
  `src/grammar.json`, and `src/node-types.json`.
- `src/scanner.c` is a hand-written external scanner (strings, heredocs, POD,
  signatures, etc.) and is **not** generated.
- Zed compiles `src/parser.c` + `src/scanner.c` into the grammar wasm. It does
  **not** run `tree-sitter generate` and does not read `grammar.js`.
- Upstream gitignores `src/*`, so it ships no `parser.c` and cannot be built by
  Zed. Our fork force-commits `parser.c` for that reason.

So: **edit `grammar.js` (and sometimes `src/scanner.c`), regenerate, commit
both the source and the generated files, push, then bump the pinned rev in the
extension's `extension.toml`.**

---

## 2. Fixes done

All verified against the grammar's own Perl test suite (`tree-sitter test`,
199 parses, 27 pre-existing failures) with **no new failures**, plus
`test/highlight.raku` (zero parse errors) and `raku -c`.

| Rev | What | Examples |
|-----|------|----------|
| `1d13358` | Commit generated parser for Zed | (build enabling) |
| `5de6437` | `~` binary concat; `multi`/`proto`/`only` | `$a ~ $b`, `multi sub f` |
| `9a1a4ae` | Typed signatures, return types, `given`/`when` | `sub f(Int $x)`, `given $x { when 1 { } }` |
| `f905384` | Twigils + `has` attributes | `$!x`, `$.x`, `has Int $.x is rw = 0;` |
| `2414eb5` | POD stops at `=end` (nesting-aware) | `=begin pod … =end pod` |
| `070d051` | `constant`/`subset`, Whatever `*`, pointy `for`, angle subscripts | `[+]`, `subset P of Int where * > 0;`, `%h<k>` |
| `6b9a22f` | Raku `.method` calls; paren-less conditions | `$o.m(1)`, `if $x { }` |
| `b89f595` | `is`/`does`/`handles` traits; safe/meta calls; named args; sigilless vars | `class C is B`, `$x.?m`, `f(:k(1))`, `my \x` |
| `148563e` | Raku `?? !!` ternary | `$a ?? $b !! $c` |
| `bc95daf` | All phasers | `ENTER`, `LEAVE`, `FIRST`, `LAST`, `NEXT`, `CATCH`, … |
| `d4f52e9` | User-defined operators | `sub infix:<+>`, `prefix:`, `postfix:`, `circumfix:`, `term:` |
| `217e5d2` | Parameterised roles/classes | `role R[::T] { }`, `class C[::T]` |
| `a92fa33` | Reduction metaoperators | `[+]`, `[~]`, `[max]`, `[*]` |
| `20b2ffe` | Return-type correction (`-->` inside, `of`/`returns` outside) | `sub f($x --> Int)`, `sub f($x) of Int` |
| `a3c3de1` | Zip/cross + hyper metaoperators; hyper method calls | `@a Z+ @b`, `@a >>+<< @b`, `@a>>.uc` |
| `83f53a2` | `but` + anonymous roles | `$x but role { method f { } }` |
| `e4cdc0b` | Private/meta methods + `submethod` | `method !x`, `method ^x`, `submethod BUILD` |
| `5213f09` | `grammar`/`token`/`rule`/`regex` declarations | `grammar G { token TOP { \d+ } }` |
| `a44b995` | Signature param modifiers | `$a?`, `:$a!`, `where * > 0`, `is rw` |
| `be5a4c9` | Compound assignment ops | `~=`, `max=`, `min=`, `Z=`, `X=` |
| `bc34d89` | Number literals | `0o17`, `0d10`, `:16<ff>` |
| `11ef6c5` | Chained subscripts | `@a[0][1]`, `%h<a><b>` |
